/* book Worked example: Q: A three-phase CSI with 120° conduction has Id = 50 A and feeds a star-connected resistive load of 2 Ω per phase. Find (a) the rms fundamental line current, (b) the total rms line current, (c) the fundamental and total load power, and (d) the rms harmonic current and the THD.
   1. (a) I1 = (√6/π) Id = 0.7797 × 50 = 38.98 A.
   2. (b) Irms = √(2/3) Id = 0.8165 × 50 = 40.82 A.
   3. (c) Star load, so the line current is the phase current. P1 = 3 I1² R = 3 × 38.98² × 2 = 9119 W; P = 3 Irms² R = 3 × 40.82² × 2 = 10000 W.
   4. (d) Ih = √(Irms² − I1²) = √(1666.7 − 1519.8) = √146.8 = 12.12 A. THD = 12.12/38.98 = 31.1 %.
   Answer: I1 = 38.98 A, Irms = 40.82 A, P1 = 9.12 kW of P = 10.00 kW, Ih = 12.12 A and THD = 31.1 %. */
