/* book Worked example 2: Q: A single-phase capacitor-commutated CSI has Id = 20 A, load R = 10 Ω, commutating capacitor C = 20 μF and output frequency 500 Hz. The thyristors have tq = 40 μs. Find the peak load voltage, the circuit turn-off time and the safety margin.
   1. RC = 10 × 20 μF = 200 μs; T = 1/500 = 2 ms, so T/4RC = 500/200 = 2.50.
   2. Peak load voltage V0 = Id R tanh(T/4RC) = 20 × 10 × tanh 2.50 = 200 × 0.9866 = 197.3 V.
   3. tc = RC ln(1 + tanh(T/4RC)) = 200 × ln 1.9866 = 200 × 0.6864 = 137.3 μs (the long-period value RC ln 2 is 138.6 μs).
   4. Margin: tc/tq = 137.3/40 = 3.4, so the thyristors have ample time to recover.
   Answer: V0 = 197.3 V peak, tc = 137.3 μs, about 3.4 times the 40 μs turn-off time. */
