/* book exam traps: Id is the height of the current wave, not its rms: the fundamental rms is 0.78Id and the total rms 0.816Id. | A CSI needs overlap between incoming and outgoing devices, not dead time; an open circuit, not a short circuit, is the dangerous fault. | The diode with each CSI switch is in series, for reverse blocking; the VSI diode is anti-parallel, for feedback. | In the capacitor-commutated CSI, the turn-off time is RC ln 2 only when the half period is long compared with RC. | A grid-tied inverter controls its current but has a capacitor DC link, so it is a VSI, not a CSI. */
