/* book Worked example: Q: A three-level NPC inverter runs from Vdc = 600 V. Find (a) the step size and the voltage each switch blocks, (b) the pole and line voltage levels, and (c) the numbers of switches, clamping diodes and bus capacitors per leg, and what they become for a five-level leg on the same bus.
   1. (a) ΔV = Vdc/(m − 1) = 600/2 = 300 V, so each switch blocks 300 V.
   2. (b) Pole levels: +300 V, 0 and −300 V. Line levels: 2m − 1 = 5, namely +600, +300, 0, −300 and −600 V.
   3. (c) Three-level leg: 4 switches, 2 clamping diodes, and the bus has 2 capacitors shared by all legs.
   4. Five-level leg: ΔV = 600/4 = 150 V; 8 switches, (4)(3) = 12 clamping diodes and 4 bus capacitors; the line voltage has 9 levels.
   Answer: Three-level: 300 V steps and blocking, pole levels ±300 V and 0, five line levels, 4 switches and 2 diodes per leg on a 2-capacitor bus. Five-level: 150 V, 8 switches, 12 diodes, 4 capacitors. */
