/* book Worked example: Q: A rooftop solar inverter sends P = 5 kW into a 230 V, 50 Hz single-phase grid. (a) Find the rms and peak current reference at unity power factor. (b) The grid rises to 240 V; find the new current and the power a frozen reference would give. (c) At 230 V the operator asks for power factor 0.9 with the same 5 kW; find the current, the reactive power and φ*.
   1. (a) I = P/V = 5000/230 = 21.74 A rms; I* = √2 × 21.74 = 30.74 A peak.
   2. (b) I = 5000/240 = 20.83 A rms. A reference frozen at 21.74 A would give 240 × 21.74 = 5217 W, so the DC-link loop must lower I*.
   3. (c) S = P/pf = 5000/0.9 = 5556 VA; I = 5556/230 = 24.15 A rms; Q = √(S² − P²) = 2422 var; φ* = cos⁻¹ 0.9 = 25.8°.
   Answer: (a) 21.74 A rms, 30.74 A peak; (b) 20.83 A, against 5217 W if frozen; (c) 24.15 A, Q = 2422 var, φ* = 25.8°. */
